WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:05.140
Structures can be thought of as file cabinets.

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:07.415
The file cabinet has folders that contain information.

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:13.900
To refer to a folder in the cabinet, you would call it

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:15.710
by the word associated with it.

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:18.180
For example, if a file cabinet was called Data,

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:21.011
we type Data dot Name to refer to the folder in which we

00:00:21.011 --> 00:00:22.260
were going to store some data.

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:28.320
Here we are storing the word Mike in Data.Name.

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:37.190
We can add as many folders to this file cabinet

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:40.280
as we want just by typing the name of the file cabinet,

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:43.150
Data, followed by the dot symbol, and then the word we

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:45.220
want to associate with the folder.

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:47.840
This word is referred to as the field.

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:50.490
The folders themselves can contain any array.

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:54.970
They can be an array of numbers or cells or even more structures.

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:59.920
Typing Data.Lego equals redLego stores a redLego into the folder called Lego.

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:09.320
Data.Apple equals pioneerMac adds another folder named Apple and stores

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:10.870
a pioneerMac inside it.

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:18.310
Just like other arrays, arrays and structures can have multiple elements.

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:21.720
Adding a second element is like adding an extra file cabinet.

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:25.960
We can do this by typing data parentheses 1 comma 2

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:28.190
dot name equals Colin.

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:31.280
When this is done, every folder that was defined for the first structure

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:33.470
is copied over to the second structure.

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:36.350
There will already be three folders in this file cabinet.

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:39.250
The folders for Apple and Lego will be empty until we define them.

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:45.590
If we add a new folder to either element of the structure,

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:47.960
it will be added to both.

